{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/38407-van-helsing-s-legacy","id":38407,"title":"Van Helsing's Legacy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-28T13:33:23-08:00","id":38407,"title":"Van Helsing's Legacy?","content":"So we all know (hopefully) that Abraham Van Helsing was the scientist that fought Dracula and helped save Mina Harker, and in WoD there are at least three &quot;Dracula&quot; imposters. So does that mean there's a possible legacy for Van Helsing in WoD for hunters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T13:50:58-08:00","id":38414,"title":"","content":"Legitimacy seems like a strange hangup to have in a game with no canon. Moreover, does it matter whether anybody claiming to be carrying out the legacy of a famous vampire hunter is a part of a pretender's cult or the real deal? This question is pretty universal to WoD organisations, not least the Ordo Dracul.<br /> <br /> Either way, the imposters you're citing all appeared in roughly a page of a supplement that is around eight years old. Honestly the most interesting thing you can do with this is create a hunter counterpart to CFD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T15:41:52-08:00","id":38463,"title":"","content":"I'm going by the Wikipedia page - I don't want to get this post contaminated by the many <i>reinterpretations </i>- but Van Helsing isn't a vampire expert, he sees the wounds, studies them and only months later comes to conclusion that it's a vampire bite. It seems like his real strength is a genius for scientific research and an open mind.<br /> <br /> However in the WoD Dracula is a lot more powerful and important than in his original book, so in the WoD we must extend the same curtsy to Van Helsing.<br /> <br /> <br /> My suggestion is thus: Dracula decided he needed an amusing diversion from his Great Work and decided to claim another bride. Van Helsing, not yet a hunter, is called in to examine Lucy and after some significant research comes to the conlusion that she is a Vampire and destroys her (origonally he examined Lucy while she was slowly transforming into a Vampire, but it doesn't work like that in the WoD). He then gathers a Tier 1 Cell and goes after Dracula.<br /> <br /> Van Helsing is the only member of his cell to survive their first encounter with Dracula. The next time he tries he goes alone, he dosn't want any more deaths on his hands, but this time he is better prepared with one of Dracula's Banes. Though Dracula wins again he is unable to seriously harm the doctor. Like all good villains who can't kill the hero, Dracula monologues about his dream of defying God. As a devout catholic Van Helsing is naturally horrified, and though he doesn't take Dracula at his word the idea that God would inflict such a monster on the world causes a short lived crisis of faith. During this crisis he went to confess and by chance or divine intervention his confessor was part of the Malleus Maleficarum.<br /> <br /> Inside the Hammer of Witches Van Helsing became a legend for his brilliance, some of his research is still part of basic training, his devotion to God, and his single minded focus on Count Dracula. Though he could never permanently destroy the monster, he was a constant thorn in Dracula's side causing innumerous setbacks to Dracula's so called Great Work. After longer than a human lifetime Dracula was finally ready to complete his great work when Van Helsing arrived for his final battle.<br /> <br /> Over the decades Dracula had grown fond of his nemesis, not as a friend, but as a constant in his long tortuous unlife. Though Van Helsing could not defeat the monster in physical combat he was able to use that fondness to finally convince Dracula to give up his self destructive work, repent, and return to God. The Count volentarally destoryed himself, and Van Helsing, his work complete, was called to his heavenly reward.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul also tell this story, they tell it with a different ending.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T15:59:46-08:00","id":38470,"title":"","content":"Commentary<br /> <br /> So basically this idea came in a flash when I read that Van Helsing was a devout catholic. It seemed obvious that the catholicism angle is a natural foil to the Ordo's core ethos. I realised that if Dracula's archenemy is God; well if God seriously wanted him dead chances are Dracula would never have lived long enough to discover the Coils and found the Ordo.<br /> <br /> Making Van Helsing as much of a spiritual enemy as a physical enemy explains why God chose to play the long game. It is also, IMO, a bit more interesting. Hunter is full to the brim of people who shoot Vampires. A battle that spans both body and soul, and a relationship between the hunter and hunted close enough to facilitate it, is somewhat more unique and I think that uniqueness is what makes it worthy of two names that basically founded the genera.<br /> <br /> I chose to put him in the MM because, well you asked for a legacy, but even if you didn't if this was just a piece of setting fiction it would be nice to read. If the organisations know about it then there's some way for the PCs to know about it so it actually be used at the table. While the book version of Van Helsing is probably a better fit for Null Mysteriis than for the MM I gave him a bump up the Tiers to match Dracula's bump, because I'm going for the religious angle, and because the MM are the Vampire org; (ok, they might be #2 after the Cainites but the Cainites don't fit at all). That said the NM probably do have some of his writings, given who he was likely to be writing too and you could easily justify some of it getting into other people's hands.<br /> <br /> Why did I kill off his Cell? Simply because none of his Cell from the book are nearly as famous as Van Helsing. Plus I think the relationship between Van Helsing and Dracula works best when it's just the two of them.<br /> <br /> Finally that immortality. The MM says it was granted by God himself but the Ordo Dracul claim that Van Helsing used Vampire Blood to extend his life. The MM know the Ordo's version of the story and the idea of vampire blood as an explanation for why you never see other deserving hunters being granted an extended lifespan crops up a bit too often for the higher ranked priest's liking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}